From: MarsDog Vision Interaction maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] rtps: release incomplete fragment cache when writer is removed

StatelessReader stores an in-progress fragmented CacheChange on its matched
writer record. It is not part of ReaderHistory until all fragments arrive, so
writer_unmatched() cannot reclaim it. Release the payload and CacheChange when
removing the writer to avoid exhausting the reader's cache pool after repeated
writer disconnects.

--- a/src/cpp/rtps/reader/StatelessReader.cpp
+++ b/src/cpp/rtps/reader/StatelessReader.cpp
@@ -213,1 +213,11 @@ bool StatelessReader::matched_writer_remove(
+                // An incomplete fragmented sample is owned by this matched
+                // writer record, not by ReaderHistory. Reclaim it before the
+                // record is erased so repeated writer removals cannot exhaust
+                // the reader's CacheChangePool.
+                if (it->fragmented_change != nullptr)
+                {
+                    releaseCache(it->fragmented_change);
+                    it->fragmented_change = nullptr;
+                }
+
                 remove_persistence_guid(it->guid, it->persistence_guid, removed_by_lease);
